    "breadcrumb": "FAU Cyber Security Club \u003e Virtual Machines",
    "content": "A hypervisor runs the VM on top of your host OS. There are several. Pick one that fits your hardware and OS.\nOptions VirtualBox Free. Cross-platform (Windows, macOS, Linux). The most widely used option for beginners.\nWorks on almost any hardware Solid snapshot support Slightly worse performance than VMware Download VMware Workstation Pro / Fusion VMware Workstation runs on Windows and Linux. VMware Fusion runs on macOS. Both are free for personal use now.\nBetter performance than VirtualBox Better USB and GPU passthrough More polished UI VMware Workstation | VMware Fusion UTM (macOS) The best option for Apple Silicon Macs. Runs ARM and x86 VMs using QEMU under the hood.\nFree Native Apple Silicon support Slightly more setup than VirtualBox Download QEMU/KVM (Linux) QEMU is a raw emulator. KVM is the Linux kernel’s virtualization module. Together they are very powerful and very manual.\nHigh performance No GUI by default — configure from the terminal or use virt-manager Best for users already comfortable with Linux QEMU docs | virt-manager Proxmox VE A hypervisor built for running on a dedicated server or homelab machine. Not for running on your laptop.\nFree, open source Web-based management UI Supports both VMs and containers (LXC) proxmox.com Quick Comparison Tool Platform Cost Best For VirtualBox All Free Beginners VMware Workstation Win/Linux Free (personal) Intermediate VMware Fusion macOS Free (personal) macOS users UTM macOS Free Apple Silicon QEMU/KVM Linux Free Power users Proxmox Dedicated server Free Homelab How the Club Uses This TODO: Add which hypervisor the club standardizes on for lab sessions and competitions.",
    "description": "A hypervisor runs the VM on top of your host OS. There are several. Pick one that fits your hardware and OS.\nOptions VirtualBox Free. Cross-platform (Windows, macOS, Linux). The most widely used option for beginners.\nWorks on almost any hardware Solid snapshot support Slightly worse performance than VMware Download VMware Workstation Pro / Fusion VMware Workstation runs on Windows and Linux. VMware Fusion runs on macOS. Both are free for personal use now.",
