    "breadcrumb": "FAU Cyber Security Club",
    "content": "AI is not a shortcut. It is a force multiplier — and in 2024–2025, it became a genuine competitive advantage in security work.\nBy the end of 2024, LLM agents were solving 95%+ of beginner CTF challenges autonomously. In 2025, one AI system placed first at a live competition and took a $50,000 prize. An autonomous pen-testing AI reached #1 on HackerOne’s US leaderboard.\nThis section covers what AI can actually do, which models to use, how to set them up, and how to build workflows and agents for security work.\nflowchart LR A([You]) --\u003e B[Pick a model] B --\u003e C[Set up tooling] C --\u003e D[Build a workflow] D --\u003e E[Automate with agents] E --\u003e F([Compound results])",
    "description": "AI is not a shortcut. It is a force multiplier — and in 2024–2025, it became a genuine competitive advantage in security work.\nBy the end of 2024, LLM agents were solving 95%+ of beginner CTF challenges autonomously. In 2025, one AI system placed first at a live competition and took a $50,000 prize. An autonomous pen-testing AI reached #1 on HackerOne’s US leaderboard.\nThis section covers what AI can actually do, which models to use, how to set them up, and how to build workflows and agents for security work.",
